Z||000000||DecadenceR||05-24-2001||04:33 PM||||First I wanna say that you guys all seem to have great advice. Second, to the hucksters picking on the Iron Duke, as long as my stock 1984 SE 2m4 is still beating those 6 cyl. Camaros, I'm pretty happy. ;-)<P>Okay problem #1 - my speedometer. the sending gear is fine. all wires seem to be connected. when the car is running the needle stays at 0. if you move it by hand, it resists and then IMMEDIATELY drops to 0 again. When the car is off, same deal without the resistance.<P>Problem #2 - cooling fan. it just doesn't fan. I put a working fan in, replaced the switch, and the fan will not work still. Not even with the AC on. So I got creative. Ran a hot power to a 20amp switch. A ground from the switch, and another ground from the fan. then an accessory from the switch to the fan. I turned it on. it ran. Until I fried the switch 20 seconds later. I turned it off, and now the switch is frozen solid. Oh, and I used 10 gauge wire. All grounds I used are good, solid grounds and I even sanded the metal bare.<P>Any thoughts or advice would be very much appreciated.||||reg||10
Z||000001||Posthumane||05-24-2001||04:42 PM||||my fan doesn't werk either. i would check the relay at the front left of the car (under the headlight) as mine turned out to be bad tho. I replaced it with a good one, but it still doesn't run, so now i'm going to check the fan.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ken Wittlief||05-24-2001||04:45 PM||||you didnt say if the speedo is working or not. Is the problem that it is not on zero when the engine is not running? that is normal, same for the tach and other gauges, when the key is off the dash instruments point randomly.||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroJoe||05-24-2001||04:46 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DecadenceR:<BR><B>Okay problem #1 - my speedometer. the sending gear is fine. all wires seem to be connected. when the car is running the needle stays at 0. if you move it by hand, it resists and then IMMEDIATELY drops to 0 again. When the car is off, same deal without the resistance.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>As long as it works fine when the car is in motion, it's doing exactly what it is supposed to.  You didnt say whether it worked when the car was moving or not.  I belive that on all Fieros when the car is off, the tach and speedo needles wont stay at zero.  As long as they zero out when the car is turned on, and function normally otherwise, you dont have a problem.<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000004||DecadenceR||05-24-2001||04:47 PM||||I'm sorry, i meant to say that it is NOT working (speedometer)||||reg||1
Z||000005||PBJ||05-24-2001||06:32 PM||||do you have cruise control and does it work?<BR>Next<BR>yellow wire-s  and  purple wire-r  check with digital volt meter for 4000 pluses (hertz) per mile. At back of cluster connecter with cluster connected and rear wheels spinning.  If so than sounds like a bad instrument panel cluster.  It does not use ecm.<p>[This message has been edited by PBJ (edited 05-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||PBJ||05-24-2001||06:42 PM||||Cooling fan does not use ecm.  I have 86 and 8 manual only.  soooo.   access cooling fan relay at LHS frt corner of engine compartment. Has 4 wires. red, black/red, brown/white, and green/white.<BR>with ignition on. you should have power on red and brown white wires. if you jumper green/white wire to ground relay should "click" and fans should turn on. power should also now be on black/red wire to fan.||||reg||1
Z||000007||drednot||05-24-2001||06:51 PM||||fiero fans never work, just don't get caught in traffic.||||reg||1
